pan> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">garlic</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">minced</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="13"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">olive oil</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="14"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">balsamic vinegar</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="15"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac12;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">kosher salt</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="16"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac14;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">black pepper</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="17"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac14;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">fresh basil leaves</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">torn, plus more as garnish</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="18"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">4</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoons</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">of balsamic glaze</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">optional</span></li></ul></div></div>
<div id="recipe-83251-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-83251-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="83251"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-83251-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Place the chicken breasts on a cutting board and pat them dry with paper towels. Place a sheet of stretch film over the chicken and pound it to  &frac34;-inch thickness. Repeat the same process for the rest of the chicken breasts and set them aside.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-chicken-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Chicken breasts pounded with stretch film on top." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-chicken-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-chicken-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-chicken-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-chicken-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-chicken.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-chicken.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-83251-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">To make the marinade, in a large bowl, whisk together &frac12; cup of balsamic vinegar, &frac14; cup of olive oil, 1 tablespoon of honey, 1 teaspoon of Dijon mustard, 2 cloves of minced garlic, 1 teaspoon of kosher salt, and &frac12; teaspoon of black pepper.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-chicken-with-balsamic-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Side by side images showing how to make balsamic chicken marinade." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-chicken-with-balsamic-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-chicken-with-balsamic-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-chicken-with-balsamic-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-chicken-with-balsamic-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-chicken-with-balsamic.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-chicken-with-balsamic.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-83251-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Add the chicken breast to the bowl, ensuring it is fully submerged in the liquid. Cover with plastic wrap and let them sit on the counter while you work on the garnish and preheat the grill.*</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83251-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">To make the caprese garnish, place 1 cup of halved cherry tomatoes, 1 clove of minced garlic, 1 tablespoon of olive oil, 1 tablespoon of balsamic vinegar, &frac12; teaspoon of kosher salt, and &frac14; teaspoon of black pepper in a bowl. Toss to combine. Add the torn basil leaves and set them aside.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-salad-for-grilled-chicken-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Images showing how to make tomato topping." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-salad-for-grilled-chicken-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-salad-for-grilled-chicken-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-salad-for-grilled-chicken-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-salad-for-grilled-chicken-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-salad-for-grilled-chicken.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Caprese-salad-for-grilled-chicken.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-83251-step-0-4" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">When ready to cook, preheat the grill over medium-high heat, about 450&deg;F (232&deg;C). Once hot, scrape the grates to remove any food residue and oil the grates.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83251-step-0-5" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Remove the chicken breasts from the marinade, letting the excess drip off, and place them on the hot grill. Grill for about 4-5 minutes, flip, and then cook for another 3-4 minutes. Check with a meat thermometer to ensure that the internal temperature registers somewhere between 160-165&deg;F (71-74&deg;C).</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/chicken-caprese-recipe-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Images showing the grilling of the chicken breasts with mozzarella slices on top." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/chicken-caprese-recipe-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/chicken-caprese-recipe-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/chicken-caprese-recipe-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/chicken-caprese-recipe-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/chicken-caprese-recipe.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/chicken-caprese-recipe.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-83251-step-0-6" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Place the mozzarella slices (2 slices on each chicken) over the chicken breasts, turn the heat to medium-low, cover the grill, and continue to cook until the cheese is slightly melted for about 3-4 minutes.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83251-step-0-7" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">If your grill has a wire shelf on top (inside the lid), place the chicken on it to prevent further cooking (and potentially drying).</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83251-step-0-8" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Transfer the chicken breasts to a large platter and cover loosely with foil. Let them rest for 5-10 minutes.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83251-step-0-9" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Right before serving, garnish the chicken with the tomato salad we made earlier.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="233" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Grilled-chicken-mozzarella-350x233.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Grilled Caprese chicken garnished with tomatoes on a plate." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Grilled-chicken-mozzarella-350x233.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Grilled-chicken-mozzarella-768x512.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Grilled-chicken-mozzarella-400x267.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Grilled-chicken-mozzarella-150x100.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Grilled-chicken-mozzarella.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Grilled-chicken-mozzarella.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-83251-step-0-10" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">If using, drizzle it with balsamic glaze and serve while still warm.</div></li></ul></div></div>

<div id="recipe-83251-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Notes</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><ul>
<li><strong>Yield:&nbsp;</strong>This recipe makes 4 caprese chicken, which is ideal for serving 4 people. The nutritional values below are per serving and do not include the calories coming from the optional balsamic glaze.</li>
<li><b>Marinating time:</b><span> If you have more time, you can marinate the chicken in the fridge for up to 2 hours or overnight. Be sure to take it out of the fridge 30 hours before grilling so that the chicken is not super cold when it hits the hot grill.</span></li>
<li><strong>Grill pan:&nbsp;</strong>If grilling outside is not an option, you can also cook the chicken in a grill pan.&nbsp;</li>
<li><b>Baked Version:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> No grill (or grill pan)? No problem! While I love the smoky flavor of grilled Caprese chicken, the baked version is just as easy to prepare. Start by marinating the chicken as written. Then place it on a parchment-lined baking sheet and bake in a preheated 400&deg;F (204&deg;C) oven for 18-22 minutes, or until the thickest part reaches 165&deg;F (74&deg;C) on a meat thermometer. During the last 3-4 minutes, add the mozzarella slices on top so they melt evenly. Once done, spoon the fresh tomato-basil mixture over the chicken and serve while it&rsquo;s still warm and juicy.</span></li>
<li><strong><strong>Storing leftovers: </strong></strong>Place leftovers in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days. Keep the tomato-basil garnish separate to keep the chicken from getting soggy.&nbsp;</li>
